-- The frame words around a herald: `l4 nlg --lang he` renders the words the
-- linearizer supplies ("is equal to", "not", month names) from the Hebrew
-- phrasebook, and names on stderr any it has no entry for.
--
-- `AS STRING` is used because "as string" has no Hebrew entry: it is the
-- fixture's deliberate gap, so the report has something to report.
IMPORT daydate

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is large` @nlg:en the claim of %amount% exceeds the threshold
                  @nlg:he %amount% עולה על הסף
  IF amount GREATER THAN 100

#EVAL `is large` 150 EQUALS TRUE
#EVAL NOT `is large` 5
#EVAL YMD 2025 7 16
#EVAL 150 AS STRING
